Thunderjar is David's side project for benchmarking coding-agent harnesses (Claude Code, OpenCode, Cursor, etc.) by running them headlessly against fixed tasks in git worktrees, then scoring the results. The goal is to compare harnesses, models, and prompt sets against each other on repeatable tasks, with enough statistical rigour (repeated iterations, pass rates) to trust the comparisons.

This document is a pre-spec: a consolidated snapshot of the design decisions, terminology, and open risks worked through across several conversations, intended as the input for a later full spec pass with an AI."}}}]}

