{"ops": [{"op": "replace", "target": {"kind": "blocks", "ids": ["mv7z9mz74gt.37"]}, "with": {"from": {"kind": "inline", "content": "## Data architecture

Run data is split into two tiers with separate retention: a small queryable metadata store for "what was the pass rate", and a large artifact store for "what exactly did the agent do".

| Tier | Holds | Local | CI | Retention |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Metadata | Run identity, measures, standard outputs, cost, tokens, duration, provenance, image tag | `.thunderjar/local.sqlite` | Postgres, or S3 + manifest | Long (e.g. 365 days) |
| Lightweight artifacts | Result JSON, OTel trace, session JSONL, patch; keyed by iteration ID | `.thunderjar/artifacts/` | Object storage | Long |
| Container snapshots | `docker commit` image per iteration | Local Docker, pruned after push | Container registry | Short (e.g. 30 days) |

One git branch per run was rejected: tens of thousands of runs would exceed GitHub's recommended ~5,000 branches per repo.

### Snapshot policy

Lightweight artifacts are extracted for every iteration. Full container snapshots default to failing or flagged iterations only. Registries bill per unique compressed layer (around US$0.10/GB-month on AWS ECR), and each snapshot adds one small layer over a shared base image, so even tens of thousands of snapshots should cost a few dollars a month.

### Image tags

`<registry>/thunderjar-runs:<task>--<harness>--<model>--<iterationId>`, sanitised for tag rules. Tags support systematic pruning by task, model or age.

### Metadata shape (sketch)

```ts
interface IterationRecord {
  iterationId: string;
  experimentName: string;
  provenance: 'local' | 'ci';
  identity: {
    commitSha: string;
    task: { name: string; instructionHash: string };
    promptSet: { name: string; hash: string };
    harness: { name: string; version: string };
    model: string;
  };
  standardOutputs: { finalText: string; commits: { sha: string; message: string }[]; diffRef: string;
                     costUsd: number; tokens: Record<string, number>; durationMs: number; sessionId?: string };
  measures: Record<string /* measurement identity */, MeasurementResult<unknown>>; // append-only
  artifacts: { traceRef?: string; transcriptRef?: string; imageTag?: string };
  createdAt: string;
}
```

### Provenance

Local runs are ephemeral: stored only in the local SQLite file, never synced. CI runs are canonical and pushed to the shared stores. Explore and restore default to CI runs and show local runs on request. This is lifecycle tagging, not authentication."}, "as": "markdown"}}]}

