{
  "verdict": "allow",
  "rev": 45,
  "data": {
    "rev": 45,
    "xml": "<doc node='a3cd2749-82e2' rev='45'><paragraph id='mv7z9mz74gt.0' rev='1' h='443a4689' heading='1'><text id='.1'>Thunderjar Specification</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.25' h='588da410'><date id='.26' value='2026-09-26'/><text id='.27'> \u00b7 </text><mention id='.30' user='u_rDNeP9LtDuSqcJknv3N0Dg' name='David (Anthropic Super User with Root Privileges)' self='true'/></paragraph><paragraph id='.43' rev='2' h='d4b1ea57' heading='2'><text id='.44'>Overview</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.52' h='3aafe670'><text id='.53'>Thunderjar is a CLI benchmark that runs coding agents headlessly against a pinned codebase, measures what they produce, and keeps every run inspectable long after it finishes. </text><comment id='78616a85-d2b4' to='claude' answered='true'/><text id='.229'>It answers questions like \"does prompt set </text><text id='.272'><code>skills-v2</code></text><text id='.281'> beat </text><text id='.287'><code>skills-v1</code></text><text id='.296'> on this task, with Haiku in Claude Code, at a 99% pass rate?\"</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.32840' rev='14' h='46f745ab'><text id='.32841'><bold>Motivations</bold></text></paragraph><paragraph id='.32852' h='0b04402b'><text id='.32853'>A coding agent's behaviour is a non-deterministic function of four things: codebase state (C), prompt configuration (P, including AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, skills and the task instruction), model (M) and harness (H). Thunderjar holds three fixed and varies one, so a change in outcome can be attributed. Background: </text><text id='.33165'><link href='https://blacksheepcode.com/posts/coding_agent_testing'>Does this tool exist?</link></text><text id='.33186'> (Black Sheep Code, July 2026).</text></paragraph><list id='.33217' h='9e74eb91' kind='bullet'><listItem id='.33218' h='2a31d29e'><paragraph id='.33219' h='c7499c42'><text id='.33220'><bold>Diagnosing regressions.</bold></text><text id='.33243'> Prompts that work today may perform worse in six months. Re-running a banked task isolates the cause: re-run old C + old P on today's M and H to test for model or harness drift; run today's P on old C to test for prompt bloat; run old P on today's C to test whether the codebase changed.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.33531' h='1c507d6b'><paragraph id='.33532' h='aaf91043'><text id='.33533'><bold>De-risking a switch.</bold></text><text id='.33553'> Before changing model or harness (for example Claude Code to OpenCode, or Sonnet to a cheaper model), run the same tasks with only that variable changed and compare pass rate, cost and tokens.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.33746' h='26a029fd'><paragraph id='.33747' h='78bf7cb0'><text id='.33748'><bold>Measuring prompt techniques.</bold></text><text id='.33776'> Advice like \"use skills\", \"use sub-agents\" or \"keep one big session\" is untested until it is measured, the same way a performance fix is unproven without a benchmark.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.33943' h='48014656'><paragraph id='.33944' h='0c76646d'><text id='.33945'><bold>Tracking cost and speed.</bold></text><text id='.33969'> Token consumption, cost and duration are hard to see in most providers' tooling; Thunderjar records them per iteration alongside correctness.</text></paragraph></listItem></list><paragraph id='.358' rev='2' h='116cd398'><text id='.359'><bold>Goals</bold></text></paragraph><list id='.364' h='15f9702f' kind='bullet'><listItem id='.365' h='b18e1b99'><paragraph id='.366' h='defe8471'><text id='.367'>Compare harnesses, models and prompt sets on the same task from the same starting commit.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.456' h='0fe7b054'><paragraph id='.457' h='30f52e05'><text id='.458'>Run many iterations of each combination and report pass rates, cost and tokens.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.537' h='bb4cd225'><paragraph id='.538' h='f25bf5c0'><text id='.539'>Preserve each run so a developer can restore it months later and see exactly what the agent did.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.635' h='151ba45e'><paragraph id='.636' h='7dbace19'><text id='.637'>Let new measurements be applied to old runs without re-running the agent.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.710' h='ebfbc468'><paragraph id='.711' h='b153aba2'><text id='.712'>Work in two modes: scripted CI, and interactive local exploration.</text></paragraph></listItem></list><paragraph id='.778' h='5620aa18'><text id='.779'><bold>Non-goals (for the proof of concept)</bold></text></paragraph><list id='.37052' rev='20' h='2ea8c9cf' kind='bullet'><listItem id='.37053' h='e3affa03'><paragraph id='.37054' h='9d0fe29a'><text id='.37055'>Infra retry/flakiness handling, cost previews and rate-limit governance (deferred nice-to-haves).</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.37152' h='c8613fd7'><paragraph id='.37153' h='92a0e05a'><text id='.37154'>Controlling sub-agent models. Only the harness's root model is a controlled variable; delegated models are observed.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.37270' h='6624acb3'><paragraph id='.37271' h='f5fa5bae'><text id='.37272'>Multi-turn, steered tasks. Only one-shot-able tasks are Thunderjar candidates.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.37350' h='f75cc8da'><paragraph id='.37351' h='168f7a14'><text id='.37352'>Faking MCP servers. Tasks whose correct outcome is an external side effect (opening a PR, posting a message) are out of scope for now; see Deferred.</text></paragraph></listItem></list><paragraph id='.1113' rev='2' h='683e4d4d'><text id='.1114'><bold>Source of authority.</bold></text><text id='.1134'> Decisions made in the design conversations are authoritative. The </text><text id='.1201'><link href='https://github.com/dwjohnston/thunderjar'>repository</link></text><text id='.1211'> is used for context only; where they disagree, this spec follows the conversation and notes the gap. The biggest gap: the repo isolates runs with git worktrees only, while this spec runs each iteration in a Docker container.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.1436' rev='3' h='9615bd0b' heading='2'><text id='.1437'>Terminology</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.1448' h='6cca45c0'><comment id='4d2cdddc-934a' to='claude' answered='true'/><text id='.1449'>The key split is type versus instance: a </text><text id='.1490'><bold>measurer</bold></text><text id='.1498'> is reusable evaluation logic, a </text><text id='.1531'><bold>measurement</bold></text><text id='.1542'> is one configured use of it on one task.</text></paragraph><table id='.1583' rev='30' h='298225ac'><row id='.1584' rev='3' h='6029028f'><cell id='.1585' h='fe55f2c5' header='true'><paragraph id='.1586' h='c6f3bfd4'><text id='.1587'>Term</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1591' h='b7ee5ffd' header='true'><paragraph id='.1592' h='9813fafb'><text id='.1593'>Definition</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1603' h='4c4abb04' header='true'><paragraph id='.1604' h='d029f87e'><text id='.1605'>Example</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1612' h='eb659a1d'><cell id='.1613' h='9ab4d952'><paragraph id='.1614' h='4bc74b21'><text id='.1615'>Task</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1619' h='eb060c3e'><paragraph id='.1620' h='a4772ab4'><text id='.1621'>A starting commit plus a task instruction, plus the measurements that judge it. Defines what the agent does and from what state.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1749' h='45526b84'><paragraph id='.1750' h='f0075d73'><text id='.1751'><code>add-function</code></text><text id='.1763'> at commit </text><text id='.1774'><code>a1b2c3</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1780' h='45fbac67'><cell id='.1781' h='ff6815b9'><paragraph id='.1782' h='0198ab05'><text id='.1783'>Task instruction</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1799' h='f34149a5'><paragraph id='.1800' h='fa445151'><text id='.1801'>The text sent to the agent telling it what to do. Passed to harnesses as </text><text id='.1874'><code>ctx.taskInstruction</code></text><text id='.1893'>.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1894' h='46234fb7'><paragraph id='.1895' h='24c5d709'><text id='.1896'>\"Write a TypeScript function called </text><text id='.1932'><code>add</code></text><text id='.1935'>\u2026\"</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1937' h='43170f2c'><cell id='.1938' h='9e12571e'><paragraph id='.1939' h='6dd38f14'><text id='.1940'>Prompt set</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1950' h='196a9a0d'><paragraph id='.1951' h='6eec4e75'><text id='.1952'>A named, reusable action that shapes the agent's environment before the run (CLAUDE.md, skills, rules). Expressed as a shell command. Distinct from the task instruction.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2121' h='3d4a2127'><paragraph id='.2122' h='a3fed4fd'><text id='.2123'><code>snerk</code></text><text id='.2128'>: copy </text><text id='.2135'><code>base_prompt_snerk.md</code></text><text id='.2155'> to </text><text id='.2159'><code>CLAUDE.md</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.2168' h='420441ae'><cell id='.2169' h='0a944a61'><paragraph id='.2170' h='e3b5b459'><text id='.2171'>Harness</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2178' h='e6a447ee'><paragraph id='.2179' h='f0387f36'><text id='.2180'>The agent tool, invoked headlessly via a </text><text id='.2221'><code>cli</code></text><text id='.2224'> callback.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2234' h='7cbf1d01'><paragraph id='.2235' h='9a6132f1'><text id='.2236'><code>claude-code</code></text><text id='.2247'>, </text><text id='.2249'><code>opencode</code></text><text id='.2257'>, </text><text id='.2259'><code>cursor</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.2265' h='f882dfdd'><cell id='.2266' h='25336894'><paragraph id='.2267' h='5e2c614c'><text id='.2268'>Model</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2273' h='6f414b25'><paragraph id='.2274' h='5689efbd'><text id='.2275'>The harness's root model. Sub-agent models are recorded, not controlled.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2347' h='9880432d'><paragraph id='.2348' h='09d0ceca'><text id='.2349'><code>claude-haiku-4-5-20251001</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.2374' h='466a0369'><cell id='.2375' h='06989b89'><paragraph id='.2376' h='72bf6e49'><text id='.2377'>Experiment</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2387' h='8f606670'><paragraph id='.2388' h='ce8bcf8b'><text id='.2389'>A named comparison: one task plus variables. Produces one run per permutation.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2467' h='e020a1e6'><paragraph id='.2468' h='8b6868df'><text id='.2469'><code>snerk-vs-glurk</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.2483' h='d31fc486'><cell id='.2484' h='4d166187'><paragraph id='.2485' h='02db55ba'><text id='.2486'>Variables</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2495' h='c81eac91'><paragraph id='.2496' h='16e19f55'><text id='.2497'>The swept axes of an experiment: harness, model, prompt set.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2557' h='5b4562c0'><paragraph id='.2558' h='5a05fe6f'><text id='.2559'>1 harness \u00d7 1 model \u00d7 2 prompt sets = 2 runs</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.2603' h='e1f472a2'><cell id='.2604' h='793803ce'><paragraph id='.2605' h='00d60e31'><text id='.2606'>Run</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2609' h='c4c9ea6d'><paragraph id='.2610' h='de7b0e12'><text id='.2611'>One execution of a task under one permutation of variables.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2670' h='03c419a9'><paragraph id='.2671' h='b1de2d6e'><text id='.2672'><code>snerk / haiku / claude-code</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.2699' h='8ca3bdf8'><cell id='.2700' h='3aff5c26'><paragraph id='.2701' h='baf6d316'><text id='.2702'>Iteration</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2711' h='88d34bf3'><paragraph id='.2712' h='29e4fea6'><text id='.2713'>One repeat of a run, used for pass-rate statistics. Each iteration gets its own container and ID.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2810' h='0fc76875'><paragraph id='.2811' h='d2d3de27'><text id='.2812'>iteration 37 of 100</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.2831' h='d3e02618'><cell id='.2832' h='996a360f'><paragraph id='.2833' h='cc2477cf'><text id='.2834'>Measurer</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2842' h='7a76df32'><paragraph id='.2843' h='f4bdac84'><text id='.2844'>Registered evaluation logic with a config type and a value type. Built-in or user-defined.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2934' h='e2d6fce0'><paragraph id='.2935' h='e416c993'><text id='.2936'><code>grep</code></text><text id='.2940'>, </text><text id='.2942'><code>fileCreated</code></text><text id='.2953'>, </text><text id='.2955'><code>templateTest</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.2967' h='88db6d62'><cell id='.2968' h='30e8e37d'><paragraph id='.2969' h='385165e2'><text id='.2970'>Measurement</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2981' h='595284a9'><paragraph id='.2982' h='cc5592ef'><text id='.2983'>A measurer plus a specific config, declared on a task. Copied per task, never shared by reference.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.3081' h='392f33fa'><paragraph id='.3082' h='58008fa9'><text id='.3083'><code>grep</code></text><text id='.3087'> for </text><text id='.3092'><code>@ts-ignore</code></text><text id='.3102'> in </text><text id='.3106'><code>output/*.ts</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.3117' h='a168fe08'><cell id='.3118' h='0c0be59e'><paragraph id='.3119' h='ebf940f2'><text id='.3120'>Measure</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.3127' h='82312a90'><paragraph id='.3128' h='567c154d'><text id='.3129'>The value one measurement produced for one iteration: a </text><text id='.3185'><code>MeasurementResult&lt;T&gt;</code></text><text id='.3205'>.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.3206' h='bfb85270'><paragraph id='.3207' h='4f1c8247'><text id='.3208'><code>{ outcome: 'measured', data: false }</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.3244' h='f2c3e437'><cell id='.3245' h='47527d09'><paragraph id='.3246' h='6e7d50e8'><text id='.3247'>Result</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.3253' h='cab0a3da'><paragraph id='.3254' h='30b88bf9'><text id='.3255'>The set of measures for an iteration, keyed by measurement identity. Can grow after the run.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.3347' h='ec75be9f'><paragraph id='.3348' h='c226758d'><text id='.3349'>3 measures at run time, 6 after a backfill</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.3391' h='299a6869'><cell id='.3392' h='2bf21409'><paragraph id='.3393' h='c657471f'><text id='.3394'>Standard outputs</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.3410' h='0bf25743'><paragraph id='.3411' h='bcbf6edd'><text id='.3412'>Data captured from every iteration for free: final text block, commit list, changed-file diff, cost, tokens, duration.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.3530' h='c58b266b'><paragraph id='.3531' h='45c27145'><text id='.3532'><code>total_cost_usd: 0.021</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.3553' rev='30' h='2d1e6152'><cell id='.3554' rev='3' h='f2b6dc55'><paragraph id='.3555' h='0f824864'><text id='.3556'>Content hash</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.3568' rev='30' h='e4d74662'><paragraph id='.3569' h='a77155da'><text id='.3570'>A hash of the content that defines a </text><text id='.41604'>harness, </text><text id='.3607'>prompt set, task instruction or measurement. Stored with the name to prove two runs are comparable.</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.3706' rev='3' h='14811b70'><paragraph id='.3707' h='2eaeab63'><text id='.3708'><code>snerk@3f9a1c</code></text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.3720' h='e214c686'><text id='.3721'><code>MeasurementResult&lt;T&gt;</code></text><text id='.3741'> is a measure, not a verdict:</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.3770' h='5db7386d' language='ts'><text id='.3771'><![CDATA[type MeasurementResult<T> =\n  | { outcome: 'measured'; data: T }\n  | { outcome: 'skipped' }                           // could not be evaluated, e.g. no output existed\n  | { outcome: 'erroredWhileMeasuring'; error: Error } // the measurer itself threw]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.4022' h='7a610a9c'><text id='.4023'>Pass/fail is derived from a measure (for example </text><text id='.4072'><code>exitCode === expectedExitCode</code></text><text id='.4101'>), so numeric measures like token counts fit the same shape.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.4161' rev='4' h='8cfa802f' heading='2'><text id='.4162'>Core concepts</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.4175' h='aee7df16' heading='3'><text id='.4176'>Run identity</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.4188' h='d743feea'><comment id='e4008881-061c' to='claude' answered='true'/><text id='.4189'>Two iterations are comparable only when every controlled input matches. A run's identity is the tuple below; iterations share it and differ only by iteration ID.</text></paragraph><table id='.39818' rev='26' h='ab4c3c6b'><row id='.39819' h='30fc749f'><cell id='.39820' h='832b9192' header='true'><paragraph id='.39821' h='ce54f0e2'><text id='.39822'>Component</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.39831' h='662e3567' header='true'><paragraph id='.39832' h='ae12665c'><text id='.39833'>Recorded as</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.39844' h='00377463' header='true'><paragraph id='.39845' h='0b40486e'><text id='.39846'>Controlled?</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.39857' h='677d69d2'><cell id='.39858' h='d4d69c47'><paragraph id='.39859' h='340f4630'><text id='.39860'>Code</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.39864' h='9cc5dae6'><paragraph id='.39865' h='e75dd47b'><text id='.39866'>Resolved commit SHA (never the literal </text><text id='.39905'><code>HEAD</code></text><text id='.39909'>)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.39910' h='eb2dfda6'><paragraph id='.39911' h='85a39ab3'><text id='.39912'>Yes</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.39915' h='377496e5'><cell id='.39916' h='bdb1c7d1'><paragraph id='.39917' h='699ad26e'><text id='.39918'>Base image</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.39928' h='ae0b9cbb'><paragraph id='.39929' h='33bd91f5'><text id='.39930'>Image digest (</text><text id='.39944'><code>sha256:\u2026</code></text><text id='.39952'>), not a mutable tag; covers OS, runtimes such as Node or Bun, and harness CLIs</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40031' h='328925c8'><paragraph id='.40032' h='85a39ab3'><text id='.40033'>Yes</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.40036' h='dbb6edb1'><cell id='.40037' h='b2cbc01a'><paragraph id='.40038' h='0198ab05'><text id='.40039'>Task instruction</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40055' h='4d7e8fc8'><paragraph id='.40056' h='01d07d1b'><text id='.40057'>Task name + hash of the instruction text</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40097' h='cfa504e0'><paragraph id='.40098' h='85a39ab3'><text id='.40099'>Yes</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.40102' h='cbc9e930'><cell id='.40103' h='6c5264cf'><paragraph id='.40104' h='6dd38f14'><text id='.40105'>Prompt set</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40115' h='f7d508b4'><paragraph id='.40116' h='c59a1333'><text id='.40117'>Name + content hash</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40136' h='d0e0d6ea'><paragraph id='.40137' h='85a39ab3'><text id='.40138'>Yes</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.40141' h='3686fda8'><cell id='.40142' h='9b5c36be'><paragraph id='.40143' h='e3b5b459'><text id='.40144'>Harness</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40151' h='21ef144e'><paragraph id='.40152' h='39b05525'><text id='.40153'>Name + content hash of its definition folder + version string (e.g. </text><text id='.40221'><code>claude --version</code></text><text id='.40237'>)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40238' h='2289d8cc'><paragraph id='.40239' h='85a39ab3'><text id='.40240'>Yes</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.40243' h='ec585f76'><cell id='.40244' h='db1963e0'><paragraph id='.40245' h='5e2c614c'><text id='.40246'>Model</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40251' h='96b6e506'><paragraph id='.40252' h='db0933e5'><text id='.40253'>Root model ID</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40266' h='89798a73'><paragraph id='.40267' h='85a39ab3'><text id='.40268'>Yes</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.40271' h='7e1f4b6f'><cell id='.40272' h='67221f2b'><paragraph id='.40273' h='b9d3130f'><text id='.40274'>Sub-agent models</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40290' h='0c309307'><paragraph id='.40291' h='2ab7e951'><text id='.40292'>Per-span model attribution from telemetry</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.40333' h='d887519e'><paragraph id='.40334' h='4052c1ec'><text id='.40335'>No, observed outcome</text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.4726' rev='4' h='0683ad1f'><text id='.4727'>Measurements are deliberately not part of run identity. They describe how a run is judged, not how it was produced, so adding a measurement never invalidates past runs.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.4895' h='898c9326' heading='3'><text id='.4896'>Hash-based versioning</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.4917' h='72d26757'><text id='.4918'>Files may be edited freely. Thunderjar never trusts a name alone; it records name plus content hash, and treats the pair as the true identity.</text></paragraph><list id='.40355' rev='26' h='7f1f9492' kind='bullet'><listItem id='.40356' h='79d1874a'><paragraph id='.40357' h='71de24f8'><text id='.40358'><bold>Prompt sets.</bold></text><text id='.40370'> Hash the prompt set's folder (definition plus the content files it applies). </text><text id='.40448'><code>snerk@3f9a1c</code></text><text id='.40460'> and </text><text id='.40465'><code>snerk@d40e77</code></text><text id='.40477'> are different prompt sets that share a label; reports group and warn on this rather than silently merging them.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.40589' h='36b8a64e'><paragraph id='.40590' h='32ddae79'><text id='.40591'><bold>Harnesses.</bold></text><text id='.40601'> Hash the harness's folder (definition plus supporting files such as settings). Changing flags, env vars or allowed tools on </text><text id='.40726'><code>claude-code</code></text><text id='.40737'> gives a new harness identity, separate from the harness CLI's own version.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.40812' h='240e339a'><paragraph id='.40813' h='add1e5cb'><text id='.40814'><bold>Measurements.</bold></text><text id='.40827'> Identity = measurer name + hash of the measurer's source + hash of the canonical JSON config. Editing what a measurement checks produces a new identity; its old measures remain attached to the old identity.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.41034' h='ebddde71'><paragraph id='.41035' h='8742791b'><text id='.41036'><bold>Task instruction.</bold></text><text id='.41053'> Hashed separately from the task's measurements, so appending measurements to a task file does not change the task's run identity.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.41183' h='5010322c'><paragraph id='.41184' h='e795e138'><text id='.41185'><bold>Optional enforcement.</bold></text><text id='.41206'> A later strict mode can refuse a run when a name's hash differs from a pinned hash. Detection is the default.</text></paragraph></listItem></list><paragraph id='.5798' rev='4' h='d5010ba8'><text id='.5799'>Determinism is the user's responsibility. A prompt set or setup command that calls a network API or reads the clock can produce different content under one hash. Thunderjar treats this as user error, not a framework concern.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.6023' h='7b39d810' heading='3'><text id='.6024'>Measurements are copied, not shared</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.6059' h='0ebdcf40'><text id='.6060'>Each task owns its measurement configs outright. Shared named measurements (one </text><text id='.6140'><code>contains-ts-ignore</code></text><text id='.6158'> referenced by 30 tasks) were rejected: changing one would ripple through every task that uses it. If duplication becomes painful, a config-generating helper called at authoring time is acceptable, because the expanded config still lives inline in each task.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.6416' h='cc4ba46b' heading='3'><text id='.6417'>Globs over exact filenames</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.6443' h='8eeefb39'><text id='.6444'>Prefer broad globs (</text><text id='.6464'><code>output/*.ts</code></text><text id='.6475'>) for behavioural checks so agent naming choices (</text><text id='.6525'><code>isPrime.ts</code></text><text id='.6535'>, </text><text id='.6537'><code>is-prime.ts</code></text><text id='.6548'>) don't cause false failures. A specific filename in a glob is an implicit assertion that the agent named the file correctly; use it only when that is intended.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.6708' h='609e065f' heading='3'><text id='.6709'>Retroactive measurement (backfill)</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.6743' h='31c6d92e'><text id='.6744'>Because every preserved iteration can be restored, new measurements can be evaluated against old runs without spending tokens. A result is an append-only map from measurement identity to measure: backfilling D, E and F adds three entries and leaves A, B and C untouched.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.7014' h='8bfddd0c' heading='3'><text id='.7015'>Measurer authoring against a fixture</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.7051' h='bdbfe47c'><text id='.7052'>Writing a measurement is writing a test against a known filesystem state. The developer restores one finished iteration and iterates on the measurement locally until it is right, with no agent variance and no API cost. The agent run is the expensive fixture; it is produced once and reused.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.7342' rev='5' h='a2ec0412' heading='2'><text id='.7343'>File structure</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.7357' h='014e52e7'><text id='.7358'>Configuration moves from one file to a folder per concept, so each prompt set, measurer and task is its own hashable unit.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.7480' h='5dc90ef9' heading='3'><text id='.7481'>User project (the repo under test)</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.7515' rev='33' h='f7119f87' language='text'><text id='.7516'><![CDATA[my-repo/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 thunderjar/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 thunderjar.config.ts        # configure()]]></text><text id='.43641'><![CDATA[: settings shared by all environments\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 thunderjar.local.ts         # environment: storage, sync, snapshots, retention\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 thunderjar.ci.ts            # environment: same keys, CI value]]></text><text id='.41335'><![CDATA[s\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 harnesses/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 claude-code/             # whole folder is hashed\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 harness.ts           # cli, version, env callbacks\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 settings.json        # optional supporting files\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 fake/]]></text><text id='.7619'><![CDATA[\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 prompt-sets/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 snerk/                   # whole folder is hashed\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 prompt-set.ts        # name + apply callback\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 CLAUDE.md\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 snerk-v2/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 measurers/                   # custom measurers only; built-ins ship with Thunderjar\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 dbRowCount.ts\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 tasks/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 add-function.ts          # instruction, commit, inline measurements\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 is-prime/\n\u2502   \u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 task.ts\n\u2502   \u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 is-prime.test.ts.template\n\u2502   ]]></text><text id='.37500'><![CDATA[\u2514\u2500\u2500 experiments/\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 snerk-vs-glurk]]></text><text id='.8270'><![CDATA[.ts\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 .thunderjar/                     # gitignored, local-only\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 local.sqlite                 # local run metadata (ephemeral provenance)\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 artifacts/<iterationId>/     # extracted lightweight artifacts]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.8487' rev='5' h='3786e4fe'><text id='.8488'>The repo's current layout (</text><text id='.8515'><code>evaluation-sandbox/thunderjar.config.ts</code></text><text id='.8554'> plus </text><text id='.8560'><code>prompts/*.md</code></text><text id='.8572'>, results in </text><text id='.8585'><code>bench/results/</code></text><text id='.8599'>) is the starting point; it migrates to the layout above.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.8656' h='631103b4' heading='3'><text id='.8657'>Thunderjar package</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.8675' h='fc10f8ef' language='text'><text id='.8676'><![CDATA[thunderjar/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 package.json                    # bin: thunderjar \u2192 src/cli/index.ts\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 cli/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 index.ts                # argument parsing and command routing\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 commands/               # run, measure, backfill, list, restore, prune\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 tui/                    # ink components: RunnerDisplay, Explorer\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 config/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 ThunderJarConfig.ts     # builder API\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 loadProject.ts          # discovers and loads the folders above\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 hashing.ts              # content hashes for prompt sets, instructions, measurements\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 validate.ts             # e.g. experiment models \u2286 harness models\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 engine/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 permutations.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 runIteration.ts         # the per-iteration pipeline\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 standardOutputs.ts      # final text, commits, diff, cost, tokens\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 measure.ts              # evaluate measurements against a filesystem\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 measurers/builtin/          # fileCreated, grep, commandExitCode, templateTest\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 ports/                      # dependency-injection seams (interfaces)\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 ContainerRuntime.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 MetadataStore.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 ArtifactStore.ts\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 adapters/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 docker/                 # real container runtime + registry push/pull\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 sqlite/                 # local metadata store\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 fake/                   # in-memory runtime and stores for tests\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 test/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 unit/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 integration/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 fixtures/fake-harnesses/    # scripts that mimic harness output and edge cases\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 evaluation-sandbox/             # self-test project in the user-project layout\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 docs/]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.10319' rev='6' h='d4357b00' heading='2'><text id='.10320'>Configuration structure</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.10343' rev='26' h='69ec2826'><text id='.10344'>Configuration is TypeScript, and anything that could be a string is a callback receiving a context object, so new context can be added later without breaking configs (the repo's operating principle). Each folder file default-exports one definition; </text><text id='.10593'><code>thunderjar.config.ts</code></text><text id='.10613'> holds project-wide settings </text><text id='.41316'>only</text><text id='.10655'>.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.10656' rev='6' h='cfab7d57' heading='3'><text id='.10657'>thunderjar.config.ts</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.41680' rev='32' h='8658a4ab' language='ts'><text id='.41681'><![CDATA[import { ThunderJarConfig } from 'thunderjar';\n\n// Shared by every environment. Anything that differs per environment lives in thunderjar.<env>.ts\nexport default new ThunderJarConfig()\n  .configure({\n    testRunner: 'bun test',\n    harnessWorkingDirectory: '.',\n    onWorktreeCreate: () => 'git config commit.gpgsign false',\n    container: { baseImage: 'thunderjar/agents@sha256:\u2026' },\n  })\n  .construct();   // harnesses, prompt sets, tasks, measurers, experiments are discovered from their folders]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.42179' h='bb811c1e' heading='3'><text id='.42180'>thunderjar.local.ts and thunderjar.ci.ts</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.42220' h='94d9e3d8'><text id='.42221'>Environment files hold everything that should differ between where Thunderjar runs: storage, sync, snapshot policy, retention and defaults. The active environment is chosen by </text><text id='.42397'><code>--env &lt;name&gt;</code></text><text id='.42409'>, then </text><text id='.42416'><code>THUNDERJAR_ENV</code></text><text id='.42430'>, then </text><text id='.42437'><code>local</code></text><text id='.42442'>. Any name works (</text><text id='.42460'><code>thunderjar.nightly.ts</code></text><text id='.42481'>); </text><text id='.42484'><code>local</code></text><text id='.42489'> and </text><text id='.42494'><code>ci</code></text><text id='.42496'> are conventions, not special cases. The environment name is recorded on every iteration as its provenance.</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.42603' h='848c8c0a' language='ts'><text id='.42604'><![CDATA[// thunderjar.local.ts \u2014 recommended: fast, throwaway\nexport default defineEnvironment({\n  defaultIterations: 1,\n  metadata: { sqlite: '.thunderjar/local.sqlite' },\n  artifacts: { dir: '.thunderjar/artifacts' },\n  snapshot: 'failuresAndFlagged',\n  push: false,                          // nothing leaves the machine\n  retention: { containerImagesDays: 7, metadataDays: 30 },\n  explore: { showEnvironments: ['ci', 'local'] },\n});]]></text></codeBlock><codeBlock id='.43032' h='18d3c1ef' language='ts'><text id='.43033'><![CDATA[// thunderjar.ci.ts \u2014 recommended: canonical, shared, long-lived\nexport default defineEnvironment({\n  defaultIterations: 50,\n  metadata: { url: process.env.THUNDERJAR_DB_URL },\n  artifacts: { bucket: process.env.THUNDERJAR_ARTIFACT_BUCKET },\n  registry: process.env.THUNDERJAR_REGISTRY,   // e.g. an ECR repository\n  snapshot: 'failuresAndFlagged',\n  push: true,\n  retention: { containerImagesDays: 30, metadataDays: 365 },\n  passRateThreshold: 0.95,              // non-zero exit below this\n});]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.39013' rev='25' h='6893596b' heading='3'><text id='.39014'>harnesses/claude-code/harness.ts</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.39046' h='f3c360ee'><text id='.39047'>Harnesses are first-class definitions like prompt sets: one folder each, hashed as a whole. Changing the CLI flags, env vars, allowed tools, appended system prompt or any supporting file produces a new harness hash, so older and newer runs are not compared by default.</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.39315' h='4c4d9e51' language='ts'><text id='.39316'><![CDATA[export default defineHarness({\n  harnessName: 'claude-code',\n  models: ['claude-haiku-4-5-20251001'],\n  version: () => 'claude --version',\n  cli: (ctx) =>\n    `claude -p \"${ctx.taskInstruction}\" --model ${ctx.model} --output-format json ` +\n    `--allowedTools \"Write,Edit,Read,Bash\"`,\n  env: (ctx) => ({ CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY: '1', OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT: ctx.otelEndpoint }),\n});]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.39709' h='605fde38'><text id='.39710'>The fake harness used in tests is just another folder (</text><text id='.39765'><code>harnesses/fake/</code></text><text id='.39780'>) with </text><text id='.39787'><code>cli: () =&gt; 'bun fake-agent.ts'</code></text><text id='.39817'>.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.11930' rev='6' h='77454944' heading='3'><text id='.11931'>prompt-sets/snerk/prompt-set.ts</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.11962' h='7a490aa3' language='ts'><text id='.11963'><![CDATA[export default definePromptSet({\n  promptSetName: 'snerk',\n  apply: (ctx) => `cp ${ctx.promptSetDir}/CLAUDE.md CLAUDE.md`,\n});]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.12089' h='fef3604e'><text id='.12090'><code>apply</code></text><text id='.12095'> stays a general shell command. A git-based variant (</text><text id='.12148'><code>git checkout &lt;sha&gt; -- CLAUDE.md .claude/</code></text><text id='.12188'>) is equally valid; the folder hash is recorded either way.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.12247' h='c150a79c' heading='3'><text id='.12248'>tasks/add-function.ts</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.12269' rev='22' h='2c6b837f' language='ts'><text id='.12270'><![CDATA[export default defineTask({\n  taskName: 'add-function',\n  commitHash: 'a1b2c3d',              // resolved to a full SHA at run time\n  instruction: 'Write a TypeScript function called `add`\u2026 Put it in the output folder. Commit the changes.',\n  measurements: [\n    { measurerName: 'fileCreated', config: { glob: 'output/*.ts' } },\n    { measurerName: 'grep', config: { glob: 'output/**', pattern: '@ts-ignore', expect: 'absent', scope: 'worktree' } },\n    { measurerName: 'templateTest', config: {\n        templatePath: 'add.test.ts.template', outputPath: 'test/add.test.ts',\n        run: 'bun test test/add.test.ts', expectedExitCode: 0 } },\n  ],]]></text><text id='.12994'><![CDATA[\n});]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.12998' rev='6' h='1e1be854'><text id='.12999'>The commit moves from the experiment to the task, matching the terminology (task = commit + instruction).</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.13104' h='8a3d080b' heading='3'><text id='.13105'>measurers/dbRowCount.ts</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.13128' h='77b121df' language='ts'><text id='.13129'><![CDATA[export default defineMeasurer<{ table: string; min: number }, number>({\n  measurerName: 'dbRowCount',\n  evaluate: async (config, ctx) => {\n    // ctx: worktreePath, exec(), standardOutputs, harness exitCode/stdout/stderr\n    return { outcome: 'measured', data: 42 };\n  },\n});]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.13404' h='67f422a8' heading='3'><text id='.13405'>experiments/snerk-vs-glurk.ts</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.13434' h='cd2196cb' language='ts'><text id='.13435'><![CDATA[export default defineExperiment({\n  experimentName: 'snerk-vs-glurk',\n  taskName: 'add-function',\n  variables: {\n    harnesses: { 'claude-code': ['claude-haiku-4-5-20251001'] },\n    promptSets: ['snerk', 'glurk'],\n  },\n});]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.13657' h='07c52196' heading='3'><text id='.13658'>Built-in measurers</text></paragraph><table id='.13676' rev='20' h='ab507837'><row id='.13677' rev='6' h='3d65653f'><cell id='.13678' h='70868c1c' header='true'><paragraph id='.13679' h='cc2477cf'><text id='.13680'>Measurer</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.13688' h='a1672e4a' header='true'><paragraph id='.13689' h='87e89abb'><text id='.13690'>Config</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.13696' h='bab0fdf4' header='true'><paragraph id='.13697' h='ebf940f2'><text id='.13698'>Measure</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.13705' h='45f28605'><cell id='.13706' h='23287704'><paragraph id='.13707' h='a0e94d81'><text id='.13708'><code>fileCreated</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.13719' h='fd89fa2d'><paragraph id='.13720' h='28c2dec1'><text id='.13721'><code>glob</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.13725' h='8aa7cba4'><paragraph id='.13726' h='bf84d3d6'><text id='.13727'><code>boolean</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.13734' h='1d24ecf7'><cell id='.13735' h='00824668'><paragraph id='.13736' h='faefbbbf'><text id='.13737'><code>grep</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.13741' h='f01b8a1d'><paragraph id='.13742' h='3552dfa4'><text id='.13743'><code>glob</code></text><text id='.13747'>, </text><text id='.13749'><code>pattern</code></text><text id='.13756'>, </text><text id='.13758'><code>expect: 'present' | 'absent'</code></text><text id='.13786'>, </text><text id='.13788'><code>scope: 'worktree' | 'changed-files' | 'added-lines'</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.13839' h='0e5a0e65'><paragraph id='.13840' h='bf84d3d6'><text id='.13841'><code>boolean</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.13848' h='51856736'><cell id='.13849' h='914e8f54'><paragraph id='.13850' h='2372a0b9'><text id='.13851'><code>commandExitCode</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.13866' h='d66d4737'><paragraph id='.13867' h='42ebb603'><text id='.13868'><code>run</code></text><text id='.13871'>, </text><text id='.13873'><code>expectedExitCode</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.13889' h='2a26ba6f'><paragraph id='.13890' h='ba3deae6'><text id='.13891'><code>{ exitCode, stdout, stderr }</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.13919' h='b4db28b0'><cell id='.13920' h='c9b06210'><paragraph id='.13921' h='5a320bd3'><text id='.13922'><code>templateTest</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.13934' h='0f67e4b2'><paragraph id='.13935' h='19650d2f'><text id='.13936'><code>templatePath</code></text><text id='.13948'>, </text><text id='.13950'><code>outputPath</code></text><text id='.13960'>, </text><text id='.13962'><code>run</code></text><text id='.13965'>, </text><text id='.13967'><code>expectedExitCode</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.13983' h='dcb3edea'><paragraph id='.13984' h='ba3deae6'><text id='.13985'><code>{ exitCode, stdout, stderr }</code></text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.14096' h='cbf6eaae'><text id='.14097'>Pluggable measurer packs (for example database assertions) register the same way as custom measurers and are imported from npm rather than bundled into the core.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.14258' h='b65c9a51' heading='3'><text id='.14259'>Validation at load time</text></paragraph><list id='.14282' h='4c3b886b' kind='bullet'><listItem id='.14283' h='ae16f9e5'><paragraph id='.14284' h='20a3c5b6'><text id='.14285'>Every experiment model must be declared on its harness. The repo currently re-lists models per experiment without this check.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.14410' h='eb8230ef'><paragraph id='.14411' h='c86c8cb3'><text id='.14412'>Every referenced task, prompt set and measurer must exist.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.14470' h='88bf0851'><paragraph id='.14471' h='3fa717e2'><text id='.14472'>Measurement configs are validated by their measurer before any agent runs.</text></paragraph></listItem></list><paragraph id='.14546' rev='7' h='7b685f7b' heading='2'><text id='.14547'>Run execution</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.14560' h='a3a5f8ce'><text id='.14561'>Each iteration runs in its own Docker container, so iterations are isolated from each other and from the developer's workspace, and can run in parallel.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.14713' h='f4140855' heading='3'><text id='.14714'>Per-iteration pipeline</text></paragraph><list id='.34608' rev='23' h='d9b2b6b0' kind='ordered'><listItem id='.34609' rev='15' h='76c24a40'><paragraph id='.34610' h='1fc82fa8'><text id='.34611'>Resolve identity: commit SHA, base image digest, prompt set hash, instruction hash, harness version. Mint an iteration ID (UUID).</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.34740' h='d36c0f74'><paragraph id='.34741' h='975cea89'><text id='.34742'>Build or reuse the </text><text id='.34761'><bold>start image</bold></text><text id='.34772'> for this permutation: the base image (by digest), plus the repo at the task commit, plus </text><text id='.34862'><code>onWorktreeCreate</code></text><text id='.34878'>, plus the prompt set's </text><text id='.34902'><code>apply</code></text><text id='.34907'>. This is exactly what the agent sees. It is always preserved and tagged, and every iteration of the permutation shares it, so it costs one layer per permutation, not per iteration.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.35088' rev='23' h='2dbb9a0e'><paragraph id='.35089' h='a49d45a0'><text id='.35090'>Start a container from the start image.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.35178' rev='15' h='55f86a82'><paragraph id='.35179' h='1017b5b8'><text id='.35180'>Invoke the harness </text><text id='.35199'><code>cli</code></text><text id='.35202'> with telemetry env vars and a per-iteration cache namespace.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.35263' h='acd34d46'><paragraph id='.35264' h='abd58f70'><text id='.35265'>Capture standard outputs: harness JSON (</text><text id='.35305'><code>result</code></text><text id='.35311'>, </text><text id='.35313'><code>session_id</code></text><text id='.35323'>, </text><text id='.35325'><code>usage</code></text><text id='.35330'>, </text><text id='.35332'><code>total_cost_usd</code></text><text id='.35346'>), final text block, commit list with messages and hashes, diff against the task commit, duration.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.35444' h='874b3733'><paragraph id='.35445' h='f97d1faf'><text id='.35446'>Evaluate the task's measurements; store each measure keyed by measurement identity.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.35529' h='97ba0480'><paragraph id='.35530' h='1a805468'><text id='.35531'>Extract lightweight artifacts: result JSON, OTel trace, session JSONL transcript, patch.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.35619' h='efbc9725'><paragraph id='.35620' h='c8c58015'><text id='.35621'><code>docker commit</code></text><text id='.35634'> the finished container to an </text><text id='.35664'><bold>end image</bold></text><text id='.35673'> tagged with the iteration ID, if the snapshot policy selects this iteration.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.35750' h='10b66480'><paragraph id='.35751' h='64fbbd92'><text id='.35752'>Record metadata; in CI, push images and metadata to shared stores. Remove the container.</text></paragraph></listItem></list><paragraph id='.15730' rev='7' h='b5fb4b82'><text id='.15731'>The code must live in the container's own filesystem, not a bind mount: </text><text id='.15803'><code>docker commit</code></text><text id='.15816'> does not capture bind-mounted volumes, so a mounted worktree would be missing from the snapshot.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.15913' h='3cb023bc' heading='3'><text id='.15914'>Cache isolation</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.15929' h='91fa49cf'><text id='.15930'>The prompt cache lives on the provider's servers, so container isolation alone does not stop one iteration reusing another's cached prefix. Disabling caching (</text><text id='.16089'><code>DISABLE_PROMPT_CACHING=1</code></text><text id='.16113'>) was rejected because caching within an iteration is realistic and cheap. The decided mechanism is a per-iteration cache namespace via Anthropic's prompt cache key, set to the iteration ID. Whether each harness CLI exposes a way to set it is an open question (see below).</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.16385' h='e87c57f5' heading='3'><text id='.16386'>Telemetry</text></paragraph><list id='.16395' h='e668fca2' kind='bullet'><listItem id='.16396' h='17d67cd8'><paragraph id='.16397' h='adb905f9'><text id='.16398'>Claude Code, Codex and Qwen Code support OpenTelemetry natively; OpenCode does not (community plugins only). For Claude Code: </text><text id='.16524'><code>CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY=1</code></text><text id='.16554'> plus </text><text id='.16560'><code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT</code></text><text id='.16587'>; tracing is beta.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.16605' h='cc959817'><paragraph id='.16606' h='6f195c78'><text id='.16607'>Cost from telemetry is API-equivalent pricing, not a subscription bill.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.16678' h='6aec6558'><paragraph id='.16679' h='608cab78'><text id='.16680'>Prefer </text><text id='.16687'><code>modelUsage</code></text><text id='.16697'> over </text><text id='.16703'><code>usage</code></text><text id='.16708'> when sub-agents are involved; plain </text><text id='.16745'><code>usage</code></text><text id='.16750'> undercounts.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.16763' h='cf0b1dca'><paragraph id='.16764' h='b16d8b52'><text id='.16765'>Thinking content is redacted from telemetry. Full reasoning is in the session JSONL transcript; </text><text id='.16861'><code>session_id</code></text><text id='.16871'> joins a trace span to its transcript file.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.16914' h='49bd2314'><paragraph id='.16915' h='b2563107'><text id='.16916'>Claude Code has no skill-invocation telemetry yet. Reconstruct skill use by matching SKILL.md paths in file-read tool calls.</text></paragraph></listItem></list><paragraph id='.17040' h='485c3338' heading='3'><text id='.17041'>Credentials and side effects</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.17069' rev='24' h='2200e369'><text id='.17070'>Iterations must be side-effect free to be safely parallel. Real credentials that act externally (for example a GitHub token that can open PRs) are never passed into containers</text><text id='.38041'>; model API keys are the only secrets a container receives. Tasks that depend on external side effects are out of scope for the proof of concept</text><text id='.17465'>.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.17466' rev='8' h='c4a06b08' heading='2'><text id='.17467'>Data architecture</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.17484' h='e110488b'><text id='.17485'>Run data is split into two tiers with separate retention: a small queryable metadata store for \"what was the pass rate\", and a large artifact store for \"what exactly did the agent do\".</text></paragraph><table id='.17669' rev='16' h='2aed48c2'><row id='.17670' rev='8' h='ac220ec8'><cell id='.17671' h='019f41fe' header='true'><paragraph id='.17672' h='cb9e8664'><text id='.17673'>Tier</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.17677' h='8ff95458' header='true'><paragraph id='.17678' h='7f1d4110'><text id='.17679'>Holds</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.17684' h='979ff3fa' header='true'><paragraph id='.17685' h='8c31e6e7'><text id='.17686'>Local</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.17691' h='fbf6c68e' header='true'><paragraph id='.17692' h='fe8ee15b'><text id='.17693'>CI</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.17695' h='d8de2976' header='true'><paragraph id='.17696' h='3b1f58d9'><text id='.17697'>Retention</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.17706' h='4ab675a5'><cell id='.17707' h='9dfbd236'><paragraph id='.17708' h='9eddf573'><text id='.17709'>Metadata</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.17717' h='5dc5f325'><paragraph id='.17718' h='b2369a4c'><text id='.17719'>Run identity, measures, standard outputs, cost, tokens, duration, provenance, image tag</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.17806' h='01403c97'><paragraph id='.17807' h='fa6d04f5'><text id='.17808'><code>.thunderjar/local.sqlite</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.17832' h='ff955eb1'><paragraph id='.17833' h='82e6d050'><text id='.17834'>Postgres, or S3 + manifest</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.17860' h='ca2b4e55'><paragraph id='.17861' h='2c26632e'><text id='.17862'>Long (e.g. 365 days)</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.17882' h='e94cc447'><cell id='.17883' h='c3bf55e2'><paragraph id='.17884' h='f7de6669'><text id='.17885'>Lightweight artifacts</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.17906' h='d05eced8'><paragraph id='.17907' h='0641a250'><text id='.17908'>Result JSON, OTel trace, session JSONL, patch; keyed by iteration ID</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.17976' h='bbc03f42'><paragraph id='.17977' h='e2bd777e'><text id='.17978'><code>.thunderjar/artifacts/</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.18000' h='9bb83de7'><paragraph id='.18001' h='6e951742'><text id='.18002'>Object storage</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.18016' h='abfa2d8b'><paragraph id='.18017' h='d1d87c47'><text id='.18018'>Long</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.18022' rev='16' h='206e3eea'><cell id='.18023' rev='8' h='f876de2c'><paragraph id='.18024' h='85fa1a62'><text id='.18025'>Container snapshots</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.18044' rev='16' h='74ab666a'><paragraph id='.18045' h='e7745332'><text id='.18046'><code>docker commit</code></text><text id='.18059'> image</text><text id='.36893'>s: one start image per permutation (always kept), one end image per selected</text><text id='.18069'> iteration</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.18079' rev='8' h='9914263f'><paragraph id='.18080' h='813e7fd5'><text id='.18081'>Local Docker, pruned after push</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.18112' h='db3ef5eb'><paragraph id='.18113' h='a1673a5f'><text id='.18114'>Container registry</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.18132' h='1d197458'><paragraph id='.18133' h='106553f5'><text id='.18134'>Short (e.g. 30 days)</text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.43528' rev='33' h='0def8fd5'><text id='.43529'>The Local and CI columns show the recommended environment configs; each environment file can choose differently.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.18154' rev='8' h='10780d81'><text id='.18155'>One git branch per run was rejected: tens of thousands of runs would exceed GitHub's recommended ~5,000 branches per repo.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.18277' h='52496130' heading='3'><text id='.18278'>Snapshot policy</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.18293' h='0eea4cf7'><text id='.18294'>Lightweight artifacts are extracted for every iteration. Full container snapshots default to failing or flagged iterations only. Registries bill per unique compressed layer (around US$0.10/GB-month on AWS ECR), and each snapshot adds one small layer over a shared base image, so even tens of thousands of snapshots should cost a few dollars a month.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.18643' h='259832b4' heading='3'><text id='.18644'>Image tags</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.18654' h='143f6b97'><text id='.18655'><code>&lt;registry&gt;/thunderjar-runs:&lt;task&gt;--&lt;harness&gt;--&lt;model&gt;--&lt;iterationId&gt;</code></text><text id='.18723'>, sanitised for tag rules. Tags support systematic pruning by task, model or age.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.18804' h='f4bbb4ab' heading='3'><text id='.18805'>Metadata shape (sketch)</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.18828' rev='34' h='4355e9a3' language='ts'><text id='.18829'><![CDATA[interface IterationRecord {\n  iterationId: string;\n  experimentName: string;\n  ]]></text><text id='.44260'><![CDATA[environment: string;              // provenance, e.g. 'local' | 'ci']]></text><text id='.18935'><![CDATA[\n  identity: {\n    commitSha: string;]]></text><text id='.36969'><![CDATA[\n    baseImageDigest: string;]]></text><text id='.18972'><![CDATA[\n    task: { name: string; instructionHash: string };\n    promptSet: { name: string; hash: string };\n    harness: { name: string; ]]></text><text id='.41567'><![CDATA[hash: string; ]]></text><text id='.19102'><![CDATA[version: string };\n    model: string;\n  };\n  standardOutputs: { finalText: string; commits: { sha: string; message: string }[]; diffRef: string;\n                     costUsd: number; tokens: Record<string, number>; durationMs: number; sessionId?: string };\n  measures: Record<string /* measurement identity */, MeasurementResult<unknown>>; // append-only\n  artifacts: { traceRef?: string; transcriptRef?: string; ]]></text><text id='.36998'><![CDATA[startImageTag: string; endI]]></text><text id='.19516'><![CDATA[mageTag?: string };\n  createdAt: string;\n}]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.19558' rev='8' h='1c4b8ff6' heading='3'><text id='.19559'>Provenance</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.19569' rev='33' h='02c326fb'><text id='.43836'>Every iteration records the environment it ran in (</text><text id='.43887'><code>local</code></text><text id='.43892'>, </text><text id='.43894'><code>ci</code></text><text id='.43896'>, or any other name). Where its data goes, whether it is pushed, and how long it is kept come from that environment's config file, not from fixed rules. The recommended setup is local runs kept on the developer's machine with short retention, and CI runs</text><comment id='0a461c04-626f' to='claude' answered='true'/><text id='.19673'> pushed to </text><text id='.19688'>shared stores</text><text id='.44150'> as the canonical record. Explore and reports filter by environment, with defaults set per environmen</text><text id='.19771'>t. This is </text><text id='.44251'>provenanc</text><text id='.19790'>e tagging, not authentication.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.19820' rev='9' h='e7597933' heading='2'><text id='.19821'>CLI</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.19824' h='595d7bd9'><text id='.19825'>One engine, two front ends: scriptable commands for CI, and an interactive </text><text id='.19900'><code>explore</code></text><text id='.19907'> TUI for local work. Both call the same injected services, so both are equally testable.</text></paragraph><table id='.19995' rev='41' h='72f3ede5'><row id='.19996' rev='9' h='f36377eb'><cell id='.19997' h='e788cad2' header='true'><paragraph id='.19998' h='71316697'><text id='.19999'>Command</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20006' h='e521493f' header='true'><paragraph id='.20007' h='5e23ec6a'><text id='.20008'>Mode</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20012' h='fb1b8328' header='true'><paragraph id='.20013' h='c74ea9dc'><text id='.20014'>What it does</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.20026' rev='37' h='49a08d54'><cell id='.20027' rev='35' h='3fcf7996'><paragraph id='.20028' h='2f167d29'><text id='.20029'><code>thunderjar run &lt;experiment\u2026&gt; [--iterations N] [--</code></text><text id='.44328'><code>env &lt;name&gt;</code></text><text id='.20080'><code>] [--json]</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20090' rev='9' h='044e0f56'><paragraph id='.20091' h='b6c1d862'><text id='.20092'>Both</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20096' rev='37' h='d20a8def'><paragraph id='.20097' h='0c30389e'><text id='.20098'>Runs experiments. Default 1 iteration; </text><text id='.20137'><code>--iterations 100</code></text><text id='.20153'> for confidence checks. </text><text id='.20177'><code>--</code></text><text id='.44338'><code>env &lt;name&gt;</code></text><text id='.20181'> </text><text id='.44348'>selects the environment file, which decides provenance, storage, push and retention</text><text id='.20226'>. Non-zero exit when a pass-rate threshold is missed.</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.20279' rev='9' h='125f3bd6'><cell id='.20280' h='fe2dc617'><paragraph id='.20281' h='ae17fc79'><text id='.20282'><code>thunderjar measure &lt;iterationId&gt; [--task &lt;file&gt;]</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20330' h='1addb972'><paragraph id='.20331' h='8c31e6e7'><text id='.20332'>Local</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20337' h='ae9a60c3'><paragraph id='.20338' h='2d1ff80a'><text id='.20339'>Restores one iteration and evaluates the task's current measurements against it. The fast loop for authoring measurements. Results are not persisted unless </text><text id='.20495'><code>--save</code></text><text id='.20501'>.</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.20502' h='4b1b620b'><cell id='.20503' h='47f94a69'><paragraph id='.20504' h='6dc06524'><text id='.20505'><code>thunderjar backfill &lt;task&gt; [--measurement &lt;id&gt;]</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20552' h='de94c566'><paragraph id='.20553' h='b6c1d862'><text id='.20554'>Both</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20558' h='89b1e8de'><paragraph id='.20559' h='ee6e4720'><text id='.20560'>Restores every preserved iteration of a task and evaluates measurements not yet recorded for it; appends measures.</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.20674' rev='40' h='7217b341'><cell id='.20675' h='ca2befba'><paragraph id='.20676' h='17369337'><text id='.20677'><code>thunderjar list [experiments|runs] [--</code></text><text id='.44482'><code>env &lt;name&gt;</code></text><text id='.20720'><code>]</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20721' rev='9' h='94ad28b6'><paragraph id='.20722' h='b6c1d862'><text id='.20723'>Both</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20727' rev='39' h='0820a236'><paragraph id='.20728' h='4feeceac'><text id='.20729'>Lists config entries or stored runs</text><text id='.44435'>, filtered by the environment config's defaults</text><text id='.20784'>.</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.20785' rev='9' h='69539ca9'><cell id='.20786' h='288e438e'><paragraph id='.20787' h='82fcb9f2'><text id='.20788'><code>thunderjar report &lt;experiment&gt; [--json]</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20827' h='bc9f89be'><paragraph id='.20828' h='b6c1d862'><text id='.20829'>Both</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20833' h='74b32b37'><paragraph id='.20834' h='e1a91a43'><text id='.20835'>Pass rates, cost and tokens per permutation, grouped by full identity; warns when one name has several hashes.</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.20945' h='9fd329bb'><cell id='.20946' h='d984fb54'><paragraph id='.20947' h='5feb242b'><text id='.20948'><code>thunderjar restore &lt;iterationId&gt;</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20980' h='4e416730'><paragraph id='.20981' h='8c31e6e7'><text id='.20982'>Local</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.20987' h='9ecc0067'><paragraph id='.20988' h='55fb1364'><text id='.20989'>Pulls the snapshot image and starts a container for VS Code Dev Containers to attach to.</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.21077' rev='41' h='fccc123d'><cell id='.21078' h='4ad7d493'><paragraph id='.21079' h='58705b88'><text id='.21080'><code>thunderjar prune [--older-than 30d] [--</code></text><text id='.44492'><code>env &lt;name&gt;</code></text><text id='.21124'><code>]</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21125' rev='9' h='c21bd302'><paragraph id='.21126' h='b6c1d862'><text id='.21127'>Both</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21131' h='6a01ca6f'><paragraph id='.21132' h='a6352414'><text id='.21133'>Applies retention: removes images and artifacts past their tier's TTL.</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.21203' h='71136321'><cell id='.21204' h='57bb20d1'><paragraph id='.21205' h='fd5a77c6'><text id='.21206'><code>thunderjar explore</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21224' h='a9e4330a'><paragraph id='.21225' h='8c31e6e7'><text id='.21226'>Local</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21231' h='a8d362e8'><paragraph id='.21232' h='5fcd6272'><text id='.21233'>ink TUI: browse experiments \u2192 runs \u2192 iterations, view measures, trace and transcript, trigger restore or measure.</text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.21346' h='ffed180c'><text id='.21347'>The live run display follows the repo's paned-runner design: tiled ink panes per permutation, falling back to a list view when there are too many to tile. Harness output is captured, never written straight to the terminal.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.21569' rev='10' h='8d563ca8' heading='2'><text id='.21570'>Tooling used to build Thunderjar</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.21602' h='40b69f93'><text id='.21603'>Thunderjar is a Bun + TypeScript package with few dependencies; shell-outs go through </text><text id='.21689'><code>Bun.$</code></text><text id='.21694'>, as the repo already does.</text></paragraph><table id='.21721' rev='45' h='0aca5c65'><row id='.21722' rev='10' h='8d8a1632'><cell id='.21723' h='63d4f43a' header='true'><paragraph id='.21724' h='bead1be3'><text id='.21725'>Concern</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21732' h='c0f2c1be' header='true'><paragraph id='.21733' h='efa0389a'><text id='.21734'>Choice</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21740' h='34a23112' header='true'><paragraph id='.21741' h='920e413c'><text id='.21742'>Status</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.21748' h='a994d3be'><cell id='.21749' h='2b63db88'><paragraph id='.21750' h='ae0c3f10'><text id='.21751'>Runtime, package manager, test runner</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21788' h='e7943a9d'><paragraph id='.21789' h='ad4acaab'><text id='.21790'>Bun (repo built on 1.3.x; </text><text id='.21816'><code>bun test</code></text><text id='.21824'>)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21825' h='86f9c288'><paragraph id='.21826' h='8e87fe50'><text id='.21827'>In repo</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.21834' rev='45' h='6755bd2d'><cell id='.21835' rev='10' h='3ff32403'><paragraph id='.21836' h='466d0612'><text id='.21837'>Language and type checking</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21863' rev='44' h='e73761e4'><comment id='51d7ca15-4823' to='claude' answered='true'/><paragraph id='.21864' h='921c5d85'><text id='.21865'>TypeScript </text><text id='.44551'>7</text><text id='.21877'>, </text><text id='.21879'><code>tsc --noEmit</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21891' rev='45' h='17268564'><paragraph id='.21892' h='9d9c7cad'><text id='.44552'>Planned; repo currently pins ^5</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.21900' rev='10' h='1bd2d0dc'><cell id='.21901' h='b51ba6e1'><paragraph id='.21902' h='0905259b'><text id='.21903'>Interactive prompts (current CLI)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21936' h='7f39713e'><paragraph id='.21937' h='21758d24'><text id='.21938'><code>@inquirer/prompts</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.21955' h='02e6aa49'><paragraph id='.21956' h='a10adcf7'><text id='.21957'>In repo; superseded by ink for </text><text id='.21988'><code>explore</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.21995' h='af03e381'><cell id='.21996' h='4c927781'><paragraph id='.21997' h='1c6f7b7d'><text id='.21998'>TUI (run display, </text><text id='.22016'><code>explore</code></text><text id='.22023'>)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.
